\par
\b Design decisions worth knowing\b0\par
\bullet The trial banner and "Then ..." subtitles render ONLY when StoreKit reports isEligibleForIntroOffer. Apple's guidance is to merchandise an intro offer only when the customer can actually redeem it; showing "7-day free trial" to someone who already used it would be a false claim and a trust-debt item.\par
\bullet clearManualProUntil is guarded: it clears only when the stored value matches the date this device wrote for the trial. manualProUntil is ALSO the support/admin comp field, so an unguarded clear would silently revoke a human-granted comp when a trial ended. setManualProUntil likewise only ever extends, never shortens, an existing grant.\par
\bullet trial_cancelled and trial_expired are deliberately distinct moments, so a cancelled trial emits both: cancelled fires when willAutoRenew flips false (intent, still inside the window, the only point a save-offer could work), expired fires when the window actually closes. Confirm this matches how the funnel should read.\par
